# Use Cases
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/use-cases/overview

Use cases help you decide **what to build with CCIP** before choosing tools or tutorials. Each use case explains the problem it solves and when it’s the right approach.

## How to choose

- **Issuing or managing a token?** Start with **Enable a cross-chain token**.
- **Building an app that spans chains?** Choose **Build a cross-chain app**.
- **Need value and instructions delivered together?** Use **Send tokens and data cross-chain**.
- **Extending CCIP’s trust model?** Explore **Build custom cross-chain verification (CCVs)**.

Each use case links to the relevant concepts, tutorials, tools, and starter paths so you can move from exploration to execution at your own pace.

## Enable a cross-chain token

Make a token natively usable across multiple blockchains while maintaining a single canonical supply and issuer-defined controls.

This use case focuses on:

- Issuing or upgrading tokens for cross-chain use
- Preserving supply integrity across chains
- Configuring mint/burn or lock/mint behavior
- Applying rate limits, permissions, and administrative controls

**Best for:**\
Asset issuers, protocol owners, institutions

→ [Explore this use case](enable-cross-chain-token)

## Build a cross-chain app

Build applications that communicate across blockchains by sending messages, tokens, or both, with programmable logic executed on the destination chain.

This use case focuses on:

- Sending arbitrary cross-chain messages
- Transferring tokens as part of application workflows
- Reacting to events on other blockchains
- Coordinating state and actions across chains

**Best for:**\
Application developers

→ [Explore this use case](build-cross-chain-app)

## Send tokens and data cross-chain

Transfer tokens alongside structured data to trigger application logic, coordinate state, or execute multi-step workflows across chains.

This use case focuses on:

- Atomic delivery of value and instructions
- Multi-step and bidirectional workflows
- Cross-chain coordination beyond simple messaging
- Advanced application patterns

**Best for:**\
Advanced application developers

→ [Explore this use case](send-token-data-cross-chain)

## Build custom cross-chain verification (CCVs)

**Advanced / Infrastructure**

Extend CCIP by implementing custom verification logic for specialized trust, compliance, or infrastructure requirements.

This use case focuses on:

- Custom trust and verification models
- Onchain and offchain verification systems
- Compliance- or institution-specific requirements
- Extending CCIP without modifying core protocol logic

**Best for:**\
Infrastructure teams, protocol builders, institutions with custom trust requirements

→ [Explore this use case](build-custom-cross-chain-verification)

