# Overview
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/concepts/overview

This section provides a system-level orientation to Chainlink CCIP and recommended reading paths.

It separates core protocol behavior from higher-level standards built on top of CCIP.

## What is CCIP

Chainlink CCIP (Cross-Chain Interoperability Protocol) is a secure, programmable cross-chain messaging and token transfer protocol.

At a high level:

- Applications send messages across blockchains
- Token transfers are implemented as programmable cross-chain actions
- Messages and token transfers are asynchronous
- Execution is verified and enforced by decentralized oracle networks
- Applications can combine tokens and arbitrary data in a single cross-chain action
- CCIP supports multiple chains and execution environments

## How CCIP Works (Protocol Layer)

This section explains CCIP at a system level:

- Network architecture
- Message flow and delivery lifecycle
- Token transfer mechanics
- Security model and verification guarantees
- Operational constraints and limits

If you are evaluating CCIP or designing a cross-chain system, start here.

If you are ready to build, continue to Getting Started or Tutorials.

## Standards Built on CCIP

CCIP provides cross-chain messaging infrastructure.

Higher-level standards can be built on top of it.

Current standard:

- **Cross-Chain Tokens (CCT)** — a secure token standard for native cross-chain token issuance and transfer.

Learn more:

- [Cross-Chain Tokens (CCT)](/ccip/concepts/cross-chain-token/overview)

## Core Concept Areas

Protocol-level concepts:

- [How CCIP Works](/ccip/concepts/architecture/overview)
- [Security & Guarantees](/ccip/concepts/best-practices)
- [Limits, Fees, and Lifecycle](/ccip/concepts/limits-fees-lifecycle)
- [Rate Limit Management](/ccip/concepts/rate-limit-management)

Standard-specific concepts:

- [Cross-Chain Tokens (CCT)](/ccip/concepts/cross-chain-token/overview)

## Cross-Chain Token (CCT) Implementations by Chain

The following references apply specifically to the Cross-Chain Token (CCT) standard built on CCIP.

CCIP messaging behavior is consistent across chains.\
CCT implementation details vary by execution environment.

### EVM

- [Architecture](/ccip/evm/concepts/cross-chain-token/architecture)
- [Technical Reference](/ccip/evm/concepts/cross-chain-token/technical-reference)

