      https://sepolia.etherscan.io/address/0x7eE7C09F7D2b802bE7BBfFa4Aa44E80ab3245514
      Destination Chain: Avalanche Fuji (Selector: 14767482510784806043)
      Destination Pool: 0x7a64D0FDd6A299AdC3eA78f692ed58B4561F322d
      ========================================

      -----------------OTHER LOGS-----------------
     ```

  2. Configure the token pool on Avalanche Fuji:

     ```bash filename="Terminal"
      # Configure Avalanche Fuji → Ethereum Sepolia
      DEST_CHAIN=ETHEREUM_SEPOLIA \
        forge script \
        script/setup/ApplyChainUpdates.s.sol \
        --rpc-url $AVALANCHE_FUJI_RPC_URL \
        --account $KEYSTORE_NAME \
        --broadcast
     ```

     Example output:

     ```bash filename="Terminal"
      -----------------OTHER LOGS-----------------
      [Step 1] Applying chain updates to pool on Avalanche Fuji
      ✅ Chain updates applied successfully!

      ========================================
      ✅ Chain Updates Complete on Avalanche Fuji!
      ========================================
      Source Pool: 0x7a64D0FDd6A299AdC3eA78f692ed58B4561F322d
      https://testnet.snowscan.xyz/address/0x7a64D0FDd6A299AdC3eA78f692ed58B4561F322d
      Destination Chain: Ethereum Sepolia (Selector: 16015286601757825753)
      Destination Pool: 0x7eE7C09F7D2b802bE7BBfFa4Aa44E80ab3245514
      ========================================

      -----------------OTHER LOGS-----------------
     ```

  3. (Optional) Read the list of supported chains and currently configured remote pools:

     ```bash filename="Terminal"
     forge script \
       script/setup/GetSupportedChains.s.sol \
       --rpc-url $ETHEREUM_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL
     ```
</Accordion>

<Accordion title="Activate the Token Pool" number={7} startOpen={false}>
  Use the `SetPool.s.sol` script to register each token pool in the CCIP `TokenAdminRegistry`, making it the official pool for your token. This is the step that activates the pool in the CCIP protocol.

  <Aside type="note" title="Why is this step at the end?">
    By running this step after all configuration (cross-chain links, finality settings, and pool hooks), the pool is fully
    configured before it goes live. This avoids a window where the pool is registered but not yet fully set up.
  </Aside>

  <GitHubCard title="SetPool.s.sol" href="https://github.com/smartcontractkit/docs-cct-foundry/blob/main/script/setup/SetPool.s.sol" iconName="github-svg-card">
    View the pool linking script on GitHub.
  </GitHubCard>

  1. Link the token to its respective token pool on Ethereum Sepolia:

     ```bash filename="Terminal"
     forge script \
       script/setup/SetPool.s.sol \
       --rpc-url $ETHEREUM_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL \
       --account $KEYSTORE_NAME \
       --broadcast
     ```

     Example output:

     ```bash filename="Terminal"
      -----------------OTHER LOGS-----------------

      [Step 1] Setting pool for token on Ethereum Sepolia
        ✅ Pool set successfully!

        ========================================
        ✅ Pool Set Complete on Ethereum Sepolia!
        ========================================
        Token Address: 0xDd13Ba083c2cAaB52eF7217EE11a90a746700CBa
        https://sepolia.etherscan.io/address/0xDd13Ba083c2cAaB52eF7217EE11a90a746700CBa
        Pool Address: 0x7eE7C09F7D2b802bE7BBfFa4Aa44E80ab3245514
        https://sepolia.etherscan.io/address/0x7eE7C09F7D2b802bE7BBfFa4Aa44E80ab3245514
        ========================================

        -----------------OTHER LOGS-----------------
     ```

  2. Link the token to its respective token pool on Avalanche Fuji:

     ```bash filename="Terminal"
     forge script \
       script/setup/SetPool.s.sol \
       --rpc-url $AVALANCHE_FUJI_RPC_URL \
       --account $KEYSTORE_NAME \
       --broadcast
     ```

     Example output:

     ```bash filename="Terminal"
