# CCIP v2.0.0 CCIPReceiver API Reference
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/ccip-receiver

## Summary

`CCIPReceiver` is an abstract base contract for applications that receive CCIP messages on EVM chains.

It:

- Stores an immutable [Router](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/router) address
- Enforces Router-only delivery of messages
- Implements ERC165 interface detection
- Exposes `_ccipReceive` as the application override hook
- Optionally exposes `getCCVs` for per-source validation requirements

***

## Contract

`chains/evm/contracts/applications/CCIPReceiver.sol`

***

## Import

```solidity
import {CCIPReceiver} from "chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/applications/CCIPReceiver.sol";
```

***

## Inheritance

- `IAny2EVMMessageReceiverV2`
- `IERC165`

Marked `abstract`.

***

## State

### Immutables

```solidity
address private immutable i_router;
```

Configured CCIP Router allowed to call `ccipReceive`.

***

## Errors

```solidity
error InvalidRouter(address router);
```

***

## Purpose in system

`CCIPReceiver` standardizes application-side integration with CCIP by:

- Ensuring only the configured Router can deliver messages.
- Providing an atomic token-transfer + message-callback model.
- Supporting interface detection for Router dispatch behavior.
- Providing optional CCV declaration via `getCCVs`.

***

## Constructor

```solidity
constructor(address router)
```

Behavior:

- Reverts `InvalidRouter(address(0))` if `router == address(0)`
- Sets `i_router = router`

***

## External API

### supportsInterface

```solidity
function supportsInterface(bytes4 interfaceId)
  public
  pure
  virtual
  override
  returns (bool)
```

Returns true for:

- `IAny2EVMMessageReceiver`
- `IAny2EVMMessageReceiverV2`
- `IERC165`

Router behavior:

- If `false` or call reverts → only tokens transferred
- If `true` → tokens transferred and `ccipReceive` called atomically
- If contract has no code → only tokens transferred

***

### ccipReceive

```solidity
function ccipReceive(
  Client.Any2EVMMessage calldata message
)
  external
  virtual
  override
  onlyRouter
```

Entry point called by Router.

Delegates to:

```solidity
_ccipReceive(message);
```

Must not be overridden directly by derived contracts.

***

### getRouter

```solidity
function getRouter()
  public
  view
  virtual
  returns (address)
```

Returns `i_router`.

***

### getCCVs

```solidity
function getCCVs(
  uint64
)
  external
  view
  virtual
  returns (
    address[] memory requiredCCVs,
    address[] memory optionalCCVs,
    uint8 optionalThreshold
  )
```

Default implementation:

- No required CCVs
- No optional CCVs
- Optional threshold = 0

Derived contracts may override.

***

## Internal API

### _ccipReceive

```solidity
function _ccipReceive(
  Client.Any2EVMMessage memory message
)
  internal
  virtual;
```

Must be implemented by derived contracts.

***

### onlyRouter modifier

```solidity
modifier onlyRouter()
```

Reverts:

```solidity
InvalidRouter(msg.sender)
```

If caller is not `i_router`.

***

## Key internal flow / invariants

- Router gating ensures no external address can inject CCIP messages.
- `ccipReceive` is final; applications override `_ccipReceive`.
- Interface detection controls Router delivery behavior.
- If `_ccipReceive` reverts, token transfer reverts atomically.

***

## Example

```solidity
contract MyReceiver is CCIPReceiver {
  constructor(address router)
    CCIPReceiver(router)
  {}

  function _ccipReceive(
    Client.Any2EVMMessage memory message
  ) internal override {
    // Application logic
  }
}
```

***

## Related Interfaces & Contracts

- [`Client`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/client)
- [`IRouter`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-router)
- [`IAny2EVMMessageReceiverV2`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-any2-evm-message-receiver-v2)
- [`OffRamp`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/offramp)

