# CCIP v2.0.0 RateLimiter API Reference
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/rate-limiter

## Summary

`RateLimiter` implements a token bucket rate limiting mechanism used by CCIP contracts to limit throughput of value or token transfers.

Features:

- Capacity-based limits
- Per-second refill rate
- Enable/disable configuration
- Minimum wait time calculation when capacity is exceeded

The library operates on `uint128` values for storage efficiency.

***

## Library

`chains/evm/contracts/libraries/RateLimiter.sol`

***

## Import

```solidity
import {RateLimiter} from "chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/libraries/RateLimiter.sol";
```

***

## Types

### TokenBucket

```solidity
struct TokenBucket {
  uint128 tokens;
  uint32 lastUpdated;
  bool isEnabled;
  uint128 capacity;
  uint128 rate;
}
```

Fields:

- `tokens` — currently available tokens.
- `lastUpdated` — last timestamp when refill occurred.
- `isEnabled` — whether rate limiting is enforced.
- `capacity` — maximum bucket size.
- `rate` — refill tokens per second.

***

### Config

```solidity
struct Config {
  bool isEnabled;
  uint128 capacity;
  uint128 rate;
}
```

Used to configure a `TokenBucket`.

***

## Constants

```solidity
uint256 internal constant SIGNATURE_LENGTH = 64; // (not present here — no constants declared)
```

No global constants declared in this library.

***

## Functions

### _consume

```solidity
function _consume(
  TokenBucket storage s_bucket,
  uint256 requestTokens,
  address tokenAddress
) internal
```

Behavior:

1. If `!s_bucket.isEnabled` or `requestTokens == 0`, returns.
2. Refills bucket based on elapsed time.
3. Reverts:

```solidity
error TokenMaxCapacityExceeded(
  uint256 capacity,
  uint256 requested,
  address tokenAddress
);
```

If `requestTokens > capacity`.

4. Reverts:

```solidity
error TokenRateLimitReached(
  uint256 minWaitInSeconds,
  uint256 available,
  address tokenAddress
);
```

If insufficient tokens available.

***

### _currentTokenBucketState

```solidity
function _currentTokenBucketState(
  TokenBucket memory bucket
) internal view returns (TokenBucket memory)
```

Returns updated bucket snapshot reflecting refill up to `block.timestamp`.

Does not modify storage.

***

### _setTokenBucketConfig

```solidity
function _setTokenBucketConfig(
  TokenBucket storage s_bucket,
  Config memory config
) internal
```

Rules:

If `config.isEnabled`:

- `config.rate <= config.capacity`
  Else reverts:

```solidity
error InvalidRateLimitRate(Config rateLimiterConfig);
```

If disabled:

- `config.rate == 0`
- `config.capacity == 0`
  Else reverts:

```solidity
error DisabledNonZeroRateLimit(Config config);
```

On success:

- Sets capacity and rate.
- Resets tokens to full capacity.
- Updates `lastUpdated`.

***

### _calculateRefill

```solidity
function _calculateRefill(
  uint256 capacity,
  uint256 tokens,
  uint256 timeDiff,
  uint256 rate
) private pure returns (uint256)
```

Returns:

```
min(capacity, tokens + timeDiff * rate)
```

Reverts:

```solidity
error BucketOverfilled();
```

If refill computation would overflow capacity constraints.

***

### _min

```solidity
function _min(
  uint256 a,
  uint256 b
) internal pure returns (uint256)
```

Returns the smaller of `a` and `b`.

***

## Errors

```solidity
error BucketOverfilled();
error TokenMaxCapacityExceeded(uint256 capacity, uint256 requested, address tokenAddress);
error TokenRateLimitReached(uint256 minWaitInSeconds, uint256 available, address tokenAddress);
error InvalidRateLimitRate(Config rateLimiterConfig);
error DisabledNonZeroRateLimit(Config config);
```

***

## Usage context

Typical usage:

```solidity
using RateLimiter for RateLimiter.TokenBucket;

RateLimiter.TokenBucket private s_bucket;

function execute(uint256 amount) external {
  s_bucket._consume(amount, address(0));
}
```

Used primarily in:

- `TokenPool`
- Rate-limited fee accounting
- Cross-chain throughput controls

***

## Related Interfaces & Contracts

- [`TokenPool`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/token-pool)
- [`FeeTokenHandler`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/fee-token-handler)

