# CCIP v2.0.0 MessageV1Codec API Reference
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/message-v1-codec

## Summary

`MessageV1Codec` defines the canonical CCIP V1 wire format and provides encoding and decoding helpers for:

- `MessageV1`
- `TokenTransferV1`

The format is:

- Chain agnostic
- Deterministic
- Hash-stable (`keccak256(encodedMessage)` produces `messageId`)
- Used by both [OnRamp](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/onramp) (encode) and [OffRamp](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/offramp) (decode)

This library contains no storage and performs no external calls.

***

## Library

`chains/evm/contracts/libraries/MessageV1Codec.sol`

***

## Import

```solidity
import {MessageV1Codec} from "chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/libraries/MessageV1Codec.sol";
```

***

## Types

### MessageV1

```solidity
struct MessageV1 {
  uint64 sourceChainSelector;
  uint64 destChainSelector;
  uint64 messageNumber;
  uint32 executionGasLimit;
  uint32 ccipReceiveGasLimit;
  uint16 finality;
  bytes32 ccvAndExecutorHash;

  bytes onRampAddress;
  bytes offRampAddress;
  bytes sender;
  bytes receiver;
  bytes destBlob;
  bytes tokenTransfer;
  bytes data;
}
```

***

### TokenTransferV1

```solidity
struct TokenTransferV1 {
  uint256 amount;
  bytes sourcePoolAddress;
  bytes sourceTokenAddress;
  bytes destTokenAddress;
  bytes tokenReceiver;
  bytes extraData;
}
```

***

### EncodingErrorLocation

Enum identifying the specific failure point during encoding/decoding.

Used by `InvalidDataLength`.

***

## Constants

```solidity
uint256 public constant MAX_NUMBER_OF_TOKENS = 1;
```

```solidity
uint256 public constant MESSAGE_V1_BASE_SIZE = ...;
uint256 public constant MESSAGE_V1_EVM_SOURCE_BASE_SIZE = ...;
uint256 public constant MESSAGE_V1_REMOTE_CHAIN_ADDRESSES = ...;
uint256 public constant TOKEN_TRANSFER_V1_BASE_SIZE = ...;
uint256 public constant TOKEN_TRANSFER_V1_EVM_SOURCE_BASE_SIZE = ...;
```

(All values match canonical source.)

***

## Errors

```solidity
error InvalidDataLength(EncodingErrorLocation location);
error InvalidEncodingVersion(uint8 version);
```

***

## Functions

### _computeCCVAndExecutorHash

```solidity
function _computeCCVAndExecutorHash(
  address[] memory ccvs,
  address executor
) internal pure returns (bytes32)
```

Computes keccak256 hash of:

```
[1-byte address length prefix]
[20-byte CCV addresses...]
[20-byte executor address]
```

***

### _encodeTokenTransferV1

```solidity
function _encodeTokenTransferV1(
  TokenTransferV1 memory tokenTransfer
) internal pure returns (bytes memory)
```

Encodes a V1 token transfer.

Reverts `InvalidDataLength` on overflow or invalid length.

***

### _decodeTokenTransferV1

```solidity
function _decodeTokenTransferV1(
  bytes calldata encoded,
  uint256 offset
) internal pure returns (TokenTransferV1 memory, uint256)
```

Decodes a token transfer starting at `offset`.

Reverts if malformed or version != 1.

***

### _encodeMessageV1

```solidity
function _encodeMessageV1(
  MessageV1 memory message
) internal pure returns (bytes memory)
```

Encodes full V1 message.

Validations:

- `tokenTransfer.length <= MAX_NUMBER_OF_TOKENS`
- Version fixed to 1
- Length prefixes must fit bounds

***

### _decodeMessageV1

```solidity
function _decodeMessageV1(
  bytes calldata encoded
) internal pure returns (MessageV1 memory)
```

Decoding steps:

1. Validate minimum length
2. Validate version == 1
3. Parse fixed header
4. Parse variable sections
5. Decode token transfer if present
6. Ensure final offset == encoded.length

Reverts with precise `EncodingErrorLocation`.

***

## Usage context

Typical usage:

```solidity
bytes memory encoded = MessageV1Codec._encodeMessageV1(message);
bytes32 messageId = keccak256(encoded);

MessageV1Codec.MessageV1 memory decoded =
  MessageV1Codec._decodeMessageV1(encoded);
```

Used by:

- OnRamp (message construction)
- OffRamp (message validation and decoding)
- TokenPool (payload parsing)

***

## Related Interfaces & Contracts

- [`OnRamp`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/onramp)
- [`OffRamp`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/offramp)
- [`TokenPool`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/token-pool)
- [`ExtraArgsCodec`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/extra-args-codec)
- [`CCVConfigValidation`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/ccv-config-validation)

