# CCIP v2.0.0 FeeTokenHandler Library API Reference
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/fee-token-handler

`FeeTokenHandler` is a minimal internal utility library used by CCIP contracts to withdraw accumulated ERC-20 fee balances.

It is used by:

- `TokenPool`
- `USDCTokenPoolProxy`
- `Executor`
- `TokenPoolFactory` (where applicable)

The library performs no access control. Calling contracts must enforce authorization.

***

## Import

```solidity
import {FeeTokenHandler} from "chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/libraries/FeeTokenHandler.sol";
```

***

## Inheritance

None — this is a Solidity library.

***

## Errors

### ZeroAddressNotAllowed()

Reverts when the provided `feeAggregator` address is `address(0)`.

***

## Events

### FeeTokenWithdrawn(address indexed receiver, address indexed feeToken, uint256 amount)

Emitted once per token transferred during withdrawal.

| Field    | Description                                |
| -------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| receiver | The address receiving the withdrawn tokens |
| feeToken | The ERC20 token address                    |
| amount   | Amount transferred                         |

***

## Structs

None.

***

## State

None — library contains no storage.

***

## Constructor

None.

***

## Internal Functions

### _withdrawFeeTokens(address[] calldata feeTokens, address feeAggregator)

Withdraws all non-zero balances of the specified tokens from `address(this)` to `feeAggregator`.

#### Parameters

| Parameter     | Type       | Description                                                |
| ------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| feeTokens     | address[] | List of ERC20 token addresses to sweep                     |
| feeAggregator | address    | Recipient of withdrawn balances (must not be zero address) |

#### Behavior

1. Reverts if `feeAggregator == address(0)`.
2. Iterates through `feeTokens`.
3. For each token:
   - Reads `balanceOf(address(this))`.
   - If balance > 0:
     - Transfers full balance to `feeAggregator` using `SafeERC20.safeTransfer`.
     - Emits `FeeTokenWithdrawn`.

#### Visibility

`internal` — must be wrapped by a public/external function in the calling contract.

***

## Usage Pattern

Typical calling contract pattern:

```solidity
function withdrawFeeTokens(address[] calldata feeTokens) external {
    // Access control enforced here
    FeeTokenHandler._withdrawFeeTokens(feeTokens, feeAggregator);
}
```

Access control is intentionally left to the caller.

***

## Security Considerations

- The library does not check caller permissions.

- The calling contract must enforce:
  - Owner-only or admin-only withdrawal.

- SafeERC20 is used to protect against non-compliant ERC20 implementations.

- Passing `address(0)` as `feeAggregator` will revert.

***

## Related Interfaces & Contracts

- [Executor](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/executor)
- [TokenPoolFactory](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/token-pool-factory)
- [TokenPool](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/token-pool)
- [USDCTokenPoolProxy](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/usdc-token-pool-proxy)

