# CCIP v2.0.0 IPoolV1 API Reference
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-pool-v1

## Summary

`IPoolV1` defines the base interface implemented by CCIP V1-compatible token pools.

Pools are responsible for:

- Removing tokens from circulation on the source chain (`lockOrBurn`)
- Delivering tokens on the destination chain (`releaseOrMint`)
- Exposing basic chain and token support queries

***

## Contract

`chains/evm/contracts/interfaces/IPoolV1.sol`

***

## Import

```solidity
import {IPoolV1} from "chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/interfaces/IPoolV1.sol";
```

***

## Interface surface

```solidity
interface IPoolV1 is IERC165 {
```

***

### lockOrBurn

```solidity
function lockOrBurn(
  Pool.LockOrBurnInV1 calldata lockOrBurnIn
)
  external
  returns (Pool.LockOrBurnOutV1 memory lockOrBurnOut);
```

***

### releaseOrMint

```solidity
function releaseOrMint(
  Pool.ReleaseOrMintInV1 calldata releaseOrMintIn
)
  external
  returns (Pool.ReleaseOrMintOutV1 memory releaseOrMintOut);
```

***

### isSupportedChain

```solidity
function isSupportedChain(
  uint64 remoteChainSelector
)
  external
  view
  returns (bool);
```

***

### isSupportedToken

```solidity
function isSupportedToken(
  address token
)
  external
  view
  returns (bool);
```

***

```solidity
}
```

***

## Integration notes / expectations

- `lockOrBurn` is called on the source chain by the OnRamp.
- `releaseOrMint` is called on the destination chain by the OffRamp.
- Implementations must enforce ramp authorization and validation internally.
- `Pool.LockOrBurnInV1` and `Pool.ReleaseOrMintInV1` structs are defined in the `Pool` library.

***

