# CCIP v2.0.0 TokenAdminRegistry API Reference
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/token-admin-registry

## Summary

`TokenAdminRegistry` is the registry contract for CCIP-enabled tokens.

It stores:

1. The configured pool for each token (`token → pool`)
2. The administrator for each token
3. A pending administrator for 2-step transfers
4. A set of registry modules authorized to propose administrators

The registry is intended to be long-lived and non-upgradable due to accumulated configuration state.

***

## Contract

`chains/evm/contracts/tokenAdminRegistry/TokenAdminRegistry.sol`

***

## Import

```solidity
import {TokenAdminRegistry} from "chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/tokenAdminRegistry/TokenAdminRegistry.sol";
```

***

## Inheritance

- `ITokenAdminRegistry`
- `ITypeAndVersion`
- `Ownable2StepMsgSender`

***

## typeAndVersion

```solidity
string public constant override typeAndVersion = "TokenAdminRegistry 1.5.0";
```

Returns:

```
"TokenAdminRegistry 1.5.0"
```

***

## State

### Constants

#### `typeAndVersion`

```solidity
string public constant override typeAndVersion = "TokenAdminRegistry 1.5.0";
```

***

### Immutables

None.

***

### Storage

#### `s_tokenConfig`

```solidity
mapping(address token => TokenConfig) internal s_tokenConfig;
```

Per-token configuration including:

- `administrator`
- `pendingAdministrator`
- `tokenPool`

***

#### `s_tokens`

```solidity
EnumerableSet.AddressSet internal s_tokens;
```

Set of all tokens ever proposed in the registry.

Tokens are never removed from this set.

***

#### `s_registryModules`

```solidity
EnumerableSet.AddressSet internal s_registryModules;
```

Set of modules authorized to propose administrators.

***

## Constructor

No constructor beyond inherited initialization from `Ownable2StepMsgSender`.

***

## External API

### Pool getters

#### `getPools`

```solidity
function getPools(address[] calldata tokens)
  external
  view
  returns (address[] memory)
```

Returns pool addresses aligned to each token input.

***

#### `getPool`

```solidity
function getPool(address token)
  external
  view
  returns (address)
```

Returns `s_tokenConfig[token].tokenPool`.

***

#### `getTokenConfig`

```solidity
function getTokenConfig(address token)
  external
  view
  returns (TokenConfig memory)
```

Returns full configuration struct.

***

#### `getAllConfiguredTokens`

```solidity
function getAllConfiguredTokens(
  uint64 startIndex,
  uint64 maxCount
) external view returns (address[] memory tokens)
```

Paginated retrieval of `s_tokens`.

Behavior:

- If `startIndex >= s_tokens.length()`, returns empty array.
- Returns up to `maxCount` entries starting at `startIndex`.

***

### Administrator functions

#### `setPool`

```solidity
function setPool(address localToken, address pool)
  external
  onlyTokenAdmin(localToken)
```

Behavior:

If `pool != address(0)`:

```
IPoolV1(pool).isSupportedToken(localToken) == true
```

Else reverts:

```
InvalidTokenPoolToken(localToken)
```

Emits:

```
PoolSet(localToken, previousPool, pool)
```

Only callable by the current token administrator.

***

#### `transferAdminRole`

```solidity
function transferAdminRole(address localToken, address newAdmin)
  external
  onlyTokenAdmin(localToken)
```

Sets:

```
pendingAdministrator = newAdmin
```

Emits:

```
AdministratorTransferRequested(localToken, msg.sender, newAdmin)
```

***

#### `acceptAdminRole`

```solidity
function acceptAdminRole(address localToken) external
```

Requires:

```
s_tokenConfig[localToken].pendingAdministrator == msg.sender
```

Else reverts:

```
OnlyPendingAdministrator(msg.sender, localToken)
```

Effects:

- `administrator = msg.sender`
- `pendingAdministrator = address(0)`

Emits:

```
AdministratorTransferred(localToken, msg.sender)
```

***

#### `isAdministrator`

```solidity
function isAdministrator(address localToken, address administrator)
  external
  view
  returns (bool)
```

Returns true if `administrator` matches stored administrator.

***

#### `proposeAdministrator`

```solidity
function proposeAdministrator(address localToken, address administrator)
  external
```

Requires:

- Caller is owner or registry module, else:

```
OnlyRegistryModuleOrOwner(msg.sender)
```

- `administrator != address(0)`, else `ZeroAddress()`
- `config.administrator == address(0)`, else `AlreadyRegistered(localToken)`

Effects:

- Sets `pendingAdministrator = administrator`
- Adds `localToken` to `s_tokens`

Emits:

```
AdministratorTransferRequested(localToken, address(0), administrator)
```

***

### Registry modules

#### `isRegistryModule`

```solidity
function isRegistryModule(address module)
  public
  view
  returns (bool)
```

Returns `s_registryModules.contains(module)`.

***

#### `addRegistryModule`

```solidity
function addRegistryModule(address module)
  external
  onlyOwner
```

Adds `module` to `s_registryModules`.

Emits:

```
RegistryModuleAdded(module)
```

Only emitted if newly added.

***

#### `removeRegistryModule`

```solidity
function removeRegistryModule(address module)
  external
  onlyOwner
```

Removes `module` from `s_registryModules`.

Emits:

```
RegistryModuleRemoved(module)
```

Only emitted if removal occurred.

***

## Events

```solidity
event PoolSet(address indexed token, address indexed previousPool, address indexed newPool);

event AdministratorTransferRequested(
  address indexed token,
  address indexed currentAdmin,
  address indexed newAdmin
);

event AdministratorTransferred(address indexed token, address indexed newAdmin);

event RegistryModuleAdded(address module);

event RegistryModuleRemoved(address indexed module);
```

***

## Errors

```solidity
error OnlyRegistryModuleOrOwner(address sender);
error OnlyAdministrator(address sender, address token);
error OnlyPendingAdministrator(address sender, address token);
error AlreadyRegistered(address token);
error ZeroAddress();
error InvalidTokenPoolToken(address token);
```

***

## Structs

### `TokenConfig`

```solidity
struct TokenConfig {
  address administrator;
  address pendingAdministrator;
  address tokenPool;
}
```

***

## Internal Functions

### `onlyTokenAdmin`

```solidity
modifier onlyTokenAdmin(address token)
```

Reverts:

```
OnlyAdministrator(msg.sender, token)
```

If:

```
s_tokenConfig[token].administrator != msg.sender
```

***

## Security model

### Trust boundaries

Owner:

- Controls registry modules.
- Can add/remove registry modules.

Registry modules:

- Can propose new token administrators.

Per-token administrator:

- Controls pool configuration.
- Can initiate admin transfer.

Pending administrator:

- Must explicitly accept role (2-step transfer).

***

### Invariants

- A token may only be registered once (`AlreadyRegistered`).
- Tokens are never removed from `s_tokens`.
- Pool assignment requires pool confirmation via `isSupportedToken`.
- Administrator transfer requires explicit acceptance.

***

## Related Interfaces & Contracts

- [`ITokenAdminRegistry`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-token-admin-registry)
- [`IPoolV1`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-pool)
- [`IPoolV2`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-pool-v2)
- [`IPoolV1V2`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-pool-v1-v2)
- [`TokenPoolFactory`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/token-pool-factory)
- [`OnRamp`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/onramp)
- [`OffRamp`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/offramp)
- [`Ownable2StepMsgSender`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/ownable-2-step-msg-sender)
- [`ITypeAndVersion`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-type-and-version)

