# CCIP v2.0.0 ITokenAdminRegistry API Reference
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-token-admin-registry

## Summary

`ITokenAdminRegistry` defines the public interface for the [TokenAdminRegistry](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/token-admin-registry).

The registry is responsible for:

- Mapping tokens to their configured CCIP pool.
- Managing per-token administrator roles.
- Supporting two-step administrator transfers.

***

## Contract

`chains/evm/contracts/interfaces/ITokenAdminRegistry.sol`

***

## Import

```solidity
import {ITokenAdminRegistry} from "chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/interfaces/ITokenAdminRegistry.sol";
```

***

## Interface surface

```solidity id="3m7kz1"
interface ITokenAdminRegistry {
```

***

### getPool

```solidity id="h6t8vx"
function getPool(
  address token
) external view returns (address);
```

Returns the pool address associated with `token`.

***

### proposeAdministrator

```solidity id="9x4tqn"
function proposeAdministrator(
  address localToken,
  address administrator
) external;
```

Proposes a pending administrator for `localToken`.

***

### acceptAdminRole

```solidity id="2v8jks"
function acceptAdminRole(
  address localToken
) external;
```

Finalizes administrator transfer for `localToken`.

***

### setPool

```solidity id="7g4lwm"
function setPool(
  address localToken,
  address pool
) external;
```

Sets the pool address for `localToken`.

***

### transferAdminRole

```solidity id="4n9pzt"
function transferAdminRole(
  address localToken,
  address newAdmin
) external;
```

Initiates transfer of administrator role for `localToken`.

***

```solidity id="v6d8jr"
}
```

***

## Integration notes / expectations

- Implementations enforce access control internally.
- Two-step administrator transfer prevents accidental ownership loss.
- Returning `address(0)` from `getPool` indicates no pool configured.
- Consumers must treat `getPool` as authoritative for pool resolution.

***

