# CCIP v2.0.0 IRouterClient API Reference
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-router-client

## Summary

`IRouterClient` defines the primary interface for applications interacting with the CCIP [Router](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/router) on EVM chains.

It allows applications to:

- Check whether a destination chain is supported.
- Quote the required fee for sending a message.
- Send cross-chain messages (with optional token transfers).

***

## Contract

`chains/evm/contracts/interfaces/IRouterClient.sol`

***

## Import

```solidity
import {IRouterClient} from "chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/interfaces/IRouterClient.sol";
```

***

## Interface surface

```solidity id="s1n7kz"
interface IRouterClient {
```

***

### Errors

```solidity id="8xk4pm"
error UnsupportedDestinationChain(uint64 destChainSelector);
error InsufficientFeeTokenAmount();
error InvalidMsgValue();
```

***

### isChainSupported

```solidity id="l9h3qv"
function isChainSupported(
  uint64 destChainSelector
) external view returns (bool supported);
```

Returns whether `destChainSelector` is supported.

***

### getFee

```solidity id="k4v2nd"
function getFee(
  uint64 destinationChainSelector,
  Client.EVM2AnyMessage memory message
) external view returns (uint256 fee);
```

Returns the fee required to send `message` to `destinationChainSelector`.

***

### ccipSend

```solidity id="m6q8rt"
function ccipSend(
  uint64 destinationChainSelector,
  Client.EVM2AnyMessage calldata message
) external payable returns (bytes32);
```

Requests the Router to send `message` to `destinationChainSelector`.

Returns the generated `messageId`.

***

```solidity id="f3k7zs"
}
```

***

## Integration notes / expectations

- `getFee` may revert for unsupported chains or malformed messages.
- If `message.feeToken == address(0)`, fees are denominated in the native token.
- `ccipSend` may revert if insufficient fee is provided.
- Overpayment of native fees is accepted and not refunded.
- Applications typically call `getFee` before `ccipSend`.

***

