# CCIP v2.0.0 IAny2EVMMessageReceiver API Reference
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-any2-evm-message-receiver

## Summary

`IAny2EVMMessageReceiver` is the base interface that application contracts must implement in order to receive CCIP messages on EVM chains.

It defines a single entrypoint:

- `ccipReceive([Client](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/client).Any2EVMMessage calldata message)`

The CCIP [Router](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/router) calls this function when delivering a cross-chain message.

***

## Contract

`chains/evm/contracts/interfaces/IAny2EVMMessageReceiver.sol`

***

## Import

```solidity
import {IAny2EVMMessageReceiver} from "chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/interfaces/IAny2EVMMessageReceiver.sol";
```

***

## Interface surface

```solidity
interface IAny2EVMMessageReceiver {
```

***

### ccipReceive

```solidity
function ccipReceive(
  Client.Any2EVMMessage calldata message
) external;
```

Called by the CCIP Router to deliver a message.

***

```solidity
}
```

***

## Integration notes / expectations

- Implementations **must verify** that `msg.sender` is the trusted CCIP Router.

- If `ccipReceive` reverts:
  - Any token transfers included in the message revert atomically.
  - The message transitions to a failed state.

- Receivers may inherit from `CCIPReceiver` to automatically enforce router validation and override `_ccipReceive` instead.

***

