# CCIP v2.0.0 IOwnable API Reference
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-ownable

## Summary

`IOwnable` defines a minimal ownership interface used by shared Chainlink access-control primitives.

It standardizes:

- Retrieving the current owner
- Initiating ownership transfer
- Accepting ownership (two-step pattern)

This interface is implemented by contracts such as `[Ownable2Step](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/ownable-2-step)` and related ownership helpers.

***

## Contract

`@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/shared/interfaces/IOwnable.sol`

***

## Import

```solidity
import {IOwnable} from "@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/shared/interfaces/IOwnable.sol";
```

***

## Interface surface

```solidity
interface IOwnable {
```

***

### owner

```solidity
function owner() external view returns (address);
```

Returns the current owner of the contract.

***

### transferOwnership

```solidity
function transferOwnership(address recipient) external;
```

Initiates an ownership transfer to `recipient`.

***

### acceptOwnership

```solidity
function acceptOwnership() external;
```

Finalizes a pending ownership transfer.

***

```solidity
}
```

***

## Integration notes / expectations

- Implementations may use a two-step ownership pattern.
- `transferOwnership` may set a pending owner rather than immediately changing ownership.
- `acceptOwnership` must be called by the proposed new owner in two-step implementations.
- This interface does not define events or errors; implementations define their own.

***

## Related Interfaces & Contracts

- [`Ownable2Step`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/ownable-2-step)
- [`Ownable2StepMsgSender`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/ownable-2-step-msg-sender)
