# CCIP v2.0.0 IOwner API Reference
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-owner

## Summary

`IOwner` is a minimal interface that exposes a single `owner()` view function.

It is compatible with standard ownership patterns (e.g., OpenZeppelin `Ownable`) and allows contracts to generically query the current owner of another contract.

***

## Contract

`chains/evm/contracts/interfaces/IOwner.sol`

***

## Import

```solidity
import {IOwner} from "chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/interfaces/IOwner.sol";
```

***

## Interface surface

```solidity
interface IOwner {
```

***

### owner

```solidity
function owner() external view returns (address);
```

Returns the address of the current owner.

***

```solidity
}
```

***

## Integration notes / expectations

- This interface only exposes a read-only ownership accessor.
- Ownership transfer mechanics are defined by the implementing contract.
- Consumers should not assume specific ownership semantics beyond the existence of `owner()`.

***

## Related Interfaces & Contracts

- [`IGetCCIPAdmin`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-get-ccip-admin)
- [`Ownable2Step`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/ownable-2-step)
- [`Ownable2StepMsgSender`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/ownable-2-step-msg-sender)
