# CCIP v2.0.0 IExecutor API Reference
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-executor

## Summary

`IExecutor` defines the interface for CCIP executor contracts.

Executors are responsible for:

- Enforcing minimum block confirmation requirements.
- Validating that they can process a given message configuration.
- Quoting a flat execution fee denominated in USD cents.

Executors are consulted during fee estimation and execution validation.

***

## Contract

`chains/evm/contracts/interfaces/IExecutor.sol`

***

## Import

```solidity
import {IExecutor} from "chainlink-ccip/chains/evm/contracts/interfaces/IExecutor.sol";
```

***

## Interface surface

```solidity
interface IExecutor {
```

***

### getMinBlockConfirmations

```solidity
function getMinBlockConfirmations()
  external
  view
  returns (uint16);
```

Returns the minimum block confirmation depth that may be requested.

***

### getFee

```solidity
function getFee(
  uint64 destChainSelector,
  uint16 requestedBlockDepth,
  address[] calldata ccvs,
  bytes calldata extraArgs,
  address feeToken
) external view returns (uint16);
```

Returns the executor fee (in USD cents) required to process the message.

***

```solidity
}
```

***

## Integration notes / expectations

- `getFee` must revert if:
  - The destination chain is unsupported.
  - The requested block depth is below the configured minimum.
  - The provided CCVs violate executor policy (if enforced).

- The returned value is denominated in USD cents (1 = $0.01).

- Downstream components convert USD cents to fee-token units.

- Executors do not themselves wait for confirmations; they only validate requested depth.

***

## Related Interfaces & Contracts

- [`Executor`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/executor)
- [`IFeeQuoter`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-fee-quoter)
- [`IPoolV2`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/i-pool-v2)
- [`OffRamp`](/ccip/evm/api-reference/v2.0.0/offramp)

