# CCIP v1.6.0 API Reference
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0
Last Updated: 2025-05-19

<Aside type="note" title="Integrate Chainlink CCIP v1.6.0 into your project">
  <Tabs sharedStore="ccip-v1-5-1-package" client:visible>
    <Fragment slot="tab.1">npm</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="tab.2">yarn</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="tab.3">foundry</Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="panel.1">
      If you use [NPM](https://www.npmjs.com/), install the [@chainlink/contracts-ccip NPM package](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@chainlink/contracts-ccip):

      ```shell
      npm install @chainlink/contracts-ccip@1.6.0
      ```
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="panel.2">
      If you use [Yarn](https://yarnpkg.com/), install the [@chainlink/contracts-ccip NPM package](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@chainlink/contracts-ccip):

      ```shell
      yarn add @chainlink/contracts-ccip@1.6.0
      ```
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="panel.3">
      If you use [Foundry](https://book.getfoundry.sh/), install the package:

      ```shell
      forge install smartcontractkit/chainlink-ccip@2114b90f39c82c052e05af7c33d42c1ae98f4180
      ```
    </Fragment>
  </Tabs>
</Aside>

<Aside type="note">You are viewing API documentation for CCIP v1.6.0, which is the latest version.</Aside>

## API References

### Core Components

- [CCIPReceiver](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/ccip-receiver) - Base contract for receiving CCIP messages
- [Client](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/client) - Library providing structs and types for building CCIP messages
- [FeeQuoter](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/fee-quoter) - Contract for managing gas and token prices in USD and calculating cross-chain fees
- [Internal](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/internal) - Library providing internal data structures and utilities for cross-chain message processing
- [IRouterClient](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/i-router-client) - Interface for sending messages through CCIP
- [Pool](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/pool) - Library providing token pool functions for cross-chain operations
- [RateLimiter](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/rate-limiter) - Contract for managing rate limits on token transfers
- [TypeAndVersion](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/i-type-and-version) - Interface for contract versioning

### Token Pools

- [BurnFromMintTokenPool](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/burn-from-mint-token-pool) - Implementation using `burnFrom(address, amount)` for token burning
- [BurnMintERC20](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/burn-mint-erc20) - Implementation for burning and minting ERC20 tokens
- [BurnMintTokenPool](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/burn-mint-token-pool) - Implementation using `burn(amount)` for token burning
- [BurnMintTokenPoolAbstract](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/burn-mint-token-pool-abstract) - Abstract contract for burn/mint token handling
- [LockReleaseTokenPool](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/lock-release-token-pool) - Implementation for locking and releasing tokens on their native chain
- [TokenPool](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/token-pool) - Base abstract class defining common functionality for all token pools

### Access Control

- [Ownable2Step](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/ownable-2-step) - Base contract implementing secure two-step ownership transfer
- [Ownable2StepMsgSender](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/ownable-2-step-msg-sender) - Extension of Ownable2Step that sets msg.sender as initial owner

### Registry Components

- [RegistryModuleOwnerCustom](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/registry-module-owner-custom) - Registry module for token admin registration
- [TokenAdminRegistry](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/token-admin-registry) - Contract for storing token pool configurations

### Events and Error Handling

- [Events](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/events) - Events emitted during CCIP operations including `ccipSend` and `ccipReceive`
- [Errors](/ccip/v1/evm/api-reference/v1.6.0/errors) - Comprehensive list of CCIP error codes and their descriptions

