# CCIP Service Limits (SVM)
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/v1/svm/concepts/service-limits
Last Updated: 2025-05-19

<Aside type="note" title="Contact for Exception Requests">
  If you consistently need more gas/Compute Units for your use case, please reach out to your Chainlink Labs point of
  contact or contact us via this [contact form](https://chain.link/ccip-contact).
</Aside>

## EVM to SVM

| Item                                  | Description                                                                                                                       | Limit        |
| :------------------------------------ | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :----------- |
| Maximum message data length           | The total payload for the message (includes the user specified message.data as well as the accounts, Bitmap, token transfer data) | 1280 bytes   |
| Message execution compute units limit | User specified compute units limit. Mandatory to be set                                                                           | 400,000 CU   |
| Maximum number of tokens              | Maximum number of distinct tokens a user can transfer in a single transaction.                                                    | 1            |
| Smart Execution time window           | Maximum duration CCIP will attempt automatic execution of message                                                                 | 8 hours      |
| Token pool execution gas limit        | Default compute units for TokenPool execution at the destination, ie., Solana                                                     | 150,000 CU   |
| Out of Order execution                | Parameter in the extraArgs of a CCIP message                                                                                      | Must be True |

## SVM to EVM

| Item                           | Description                                                                                            | Limit         |
| :----------------------------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :------------ |
| Maximum message data length    | data payload sent within the [CCIP message](/ccip/v1/svm/api-reference/v1.6.0/messages#svm2anymessage) | 400 bytes     |
| Message execution gas limit    | User specified gas limit. Mandatory to be set                                                          | 3,000,000 gas |
| Maximum number of tokens       | Maximum number of distinct tokens a user can transfer in a single transaction.                         | 1             |
| Smart Execution time window    | Maximum duration for the execution of a CCIP message                                                   | 8 hours       |
| Token pool execution gas limit | Maximum gas for executing the combined steps in token pools during cross-chain transfers               | 90,000 gas    |
| Out of Order execution         | Parameter in the extraArgs of a CCIP message                                                           | Must be True  |

---

# Build with the Solana Starter Kit
Source: https://docs.chain.link/ccip/v1/svm/getting-started/build-with-starter-kits

This page shows how **experienced Solana builders** can use the official Solana Starter Kit to jump straight into **Chainlink CCIP**-enabled development on Solana.

Starter kits are maintained repositories intended for developers who prefer starting from real, maintained code rather than step-by-step tutorials.

## Who this is for

This path is intended for developers who:

- Are comfortable with Solana programs and the Anchor framework
- Understand Rust and JavaScript/TypeScript Solana clients
- Want a working CCIP setup immediately
- Prefer learning by reading and extending real code
- Plan to customize or productionize cross-chain workflows

You do not need to follow the full tutorial sequence to use the starter kit.

## What the Solana Starter Kit provides

The Solana Starter Kit is a maintained repository that includes:

- An **Anchor-based on-chain program** and a JS/TS client
- Comprehensive **CCIP libraries and scripts** for cross-chain workflows
- Pre-configured scripts for **token transfers and arbitrary messaging** across chains
- Tools for **multi-chain support** including EVM ↔ Solana operations
- Example patterns for token pool setup, delegation, and messaging workflows
- Scripts to bootstrap CCIP operations between Solana and supported EVM networks

These kits assume familiarity with Solana program patterns and optimize for implementation speed.

## Example workflow (high level)

A typical Solana Starter Kit workflow looks like this:

1. Clone the **Solana Starter Kit** repository
2. Install dependencies and configure environment variables
3. Build and deploy the Anchor program to a Solana cluster
4. Use included **CCIP scripts** to send tokens or messages cross-chain
5. Extend program logic or scripts to support your application’s requirements

For full step-by-step instructions, follow the README and the CCIP scripts documentation within the repository.

## Solana Starter Kit — CCIP support

This starter kit includes integrated support for Chainlink CCIP workflows between Solana and EVM chains.

### Cross-Chain Interoperability Protocol (CCIP)

The CCIP section of the Solana Starter Kit enables:

- **Token Transfers**: Send tokens from EVM networks (e.g., Ethereum, Base, Arbitrum) to Solana and vice versa
- **Arbitrary Messaging**: Send custom payloads across chains
- **Token Pool Management**: Configure and operate burn-mint pools for supported assets
- **Multi-Chain Support**: Tools and scripts for both EVM and Solana workflows.

👉 **Repository:**\
[https://github.com/smartcontractkit/solana-starter-kit](https://github.com/smartcontractkit/solana-starter-kit)

## Where to go next

- Review **[Concepts](../concepts)** to understand CCIP guarantees, architecture, and execution behavior
- Use **[Tutorials](../tutorials)** to explore specific cross-chain patterns or APIs referenced in the starter kit
- Extend the starter kit implementation to build and productionize your cross-chain application

---

